# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Select an AlternateAdditionalCost branch on Bitter Triumph
#   (K:AlternateAdditionalCost:PayLife<3>:Discard<1/Card>), neither of which
#   is a Sacrifice/Exile/Blight cost — the only branch shapes the request
#   builder could previously label.
# Forcing: Grizzly Bears in hand is the only card available to discard.
# AI behavior: The scripted human path has one spell target and one cost choice.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN = the spell and the selected additional-cost branch resolve normally.
#   LOSE = the cast, cost-choice, or targeting prompt did not resume the game.
#   TIMEOUT = the CastingTimeOptionsReq never receives a client response — the
#     defect this fixture guards: an unlabeled SelectNReq option index throws
#     client-side (CastingTimeOption_ChooseOrCostRequest indexes straight into
#     Prompt.Parameters with no bounds check) and hangs the match.
# Card roles:
#   Bitter Triumph — exposes the PayLife-or-Discard additional-cost branch.
#   Grizzly Bears — the only discardable card; also proves the hand size drops.
#   Centaur Courser — deterministic destroy target.
# Protocol path: Cast, CastingTimeOptionsReq, SelectTargetsReq, CastingTimeOption.
[metadata]
Name:Bitter Triumph Alternate Cost
Goal:Win
Turns:2
Difficulty:Easy
Description:Choose an additional-cost branch and destroy Centaur Courser.

[state]
ActivePlayer=Human
ActivePhase=Main1
HumanLife=20
AILife=20

humanhand=Bitter Triumph;Grizzly Bears
humanbattlefield=Swamp;Swamp
humanlibrary=Swamp
aibattlefield=Centaur Courser
ailibrary=Mountain
